IMPORT prelude

-- Deep Seabed Mining Act 2015 (Singapore) -- who may not mine the deep seabed and the exceptions (ss 2, 4, 5), who may hold and
-- receive a licence (ss 6(3), 7, 12(2), 25), when a licence lapses or may be suspended or revoked (ss 13, 14), the timetable for
-- representations (s 15), the wind-down directions and who may receive them (s 16), financial penalties (ss 10(4), 11(3), 16(5),
-- 24(2)(g)) and officers' liability (s 21).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DSMA2015.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the body is [40/2019], on the definition of "Singapore national" in s 2.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0119 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the prohibition, its exceptions, licence eligibility and loss, the s 15 and s 16 procedures, and the
-- penalties. Not encoded: the Minister's discretion over licence content and conditions (ss 6(1), (2), 8, 9, 10(1)-(3), 11(1),
-- (2), (4)), the Court's remedies for wrongful acts under Annex III, Article 22 (s 17), registration and enforcement of Seabed
-- Disputes Chamber decisions and arbitral awards (ss 18-20), recovery of penalties as fines (s 22), Rules of Court and the
-- regulation-making power beyond s 24(2)(g) (ss 23, 24), and anything in the Convention, the Agreement or ISA rules themselves.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Deep Seabed Mining Act 2015 -- mining in the Area`

-- s 2: "Singapore national" means "(a) a Singapore citizen; or (b) an entity incorporated, formed or established in Singapore
-- under any written law" [40/2019]. "Singapore company" means "a company incorporated in Singapore". "Area" means "the seabed
-- and ocean floor, and the subsoil thereof, beyond the limits of any national jurisdiction".
-- INFERENCE: a Singapore limited liability partnership is taken to be an entity "formed or established in Singapore under any
-- written law"; s 2 does not name it.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore citizen`
    `a Singapore permanent resident who is not a citizen`
    `a foreign individual`
    `a Singapore company`
    `a Singapore limited liability partnership`
    `a foreign company`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor is a Singapore national` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `a Singapore citizen` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Singapore company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Singapore limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor is an individual` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `a Singapore citizen` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Singapore permanent resident who is not a citizen` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a foreign individual` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4, 5 -- the prohibition and its exceptions`

-- s 4(1): "Except as provided in section 5, a Singapore national must not explore for or exploit any resource in the Area."
-- s 5(1): a Singapore company may if (a) it "has been granted a licence to explore for or exploit that type of resource in that
-- part of the Area"; (b) the licence "remains in force"; (c) it "has entered into a corresponding ISA contract"; and (d) that
-- contract "remains in force".
-- s 5(2): "An individual who is a Singapore citizen" may if (a) acting as employee or agent of (i) a Singapore company meeting
-- s 5(1), or (ii) "a person who has entered into an ISA contract under the sponsorship of any State other than Singapore, and
-- the ISA contract remains in force"; and (b) the activities are "within the scope of" that licence or that ISA contract.
-- There is no exception for a Singapore entity other than a company, and none for a Singapore company sponsored by another State.
DECLARE Activity HAS
    `who` IS AN Actor
    `holds a licence for that resource in that part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licence is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a corresponding ISA contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ISA contract is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works for a Singapore company meeting section 5(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within that company's licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works for a contractor sponsored by another State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that contractor's ISA contract is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within that contractor's ISA contract` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company exception applies` IF
        `the activity`'s `who` EQUALS `a Singapore company`
    AND `the activity`'s `holds a licence for that resource in that part`
    AND `the activity`'s `the licence is in force`
    AND `the activity`'s `has a corresponding ISA contract`
    AND `the activity`'s `the ISA contract is in force`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the citizen exception applies` IF
        `the activity`'s `who` EQUALS `a Singapore citizen`
    AND (    (`the activity`'s `works for a Singapore company meeting section 5(1)` AND `the activity`'s `within that company's licence`)
         OR  (    `the activity`'s `works for a contractor sponsored by another State`
              AND `the activity`'s `that contractor's ISA contract is in force`
              AND `the activity`'s `within that contractor's ISA contract`))

-- s 4(2): a contravention "shall be guilty of an offence".
GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exploring or exploiting is an offence` IF
        `the actor is a Singapore national` (`the activity`'s `who`)
    AND (NOT `the company exception applies` `the activity`)
    AND (NOT `the citizen exception applies` `the activity`)

§§ `4(2) -- punishment`

-- s 4(2)(a), individuals: "a fine not exceeding $300,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or to both" and,
-- for a continuing offence, "a further fine not exceeding $50,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- continues after conviction, but not exceeding $500,000 in total". (b) any other case: the same fines, no imprisonment.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the actor is an individual` `the actor` THEN 3 ELSE 0

-- `days continued` counts each day or part of a day after conviction.
GIVEN `days continued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum further fine` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`days continued` TIMES 50000) 500000

GIVEN `days continued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine` MEANS
    300000 PLUS `the maximum further fine` `days continued`

§§ `6(3), 7, 12(2), 25 -- who may hold a licence`

-- s 6(3): "A licence must relate to only one type of resource."
GIVEN `number of resource types` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a licence may cover that many resource types` IF
    `number of resource types` EQUALS 1

-- s 7(1): "Only a Singapore company may apply for and be granted a licence." (2): it "may be granted more than one licence".
-- (3): the Minister "must be satisfied that" (a) the company "meets, or is likely to meet, the qualification standards under
-- Annex III, Article 4 of the Convention"; (b) it "will be applying to the ISA to enter into a corresponding ISA contract"; (c) "it
-- is in Singapore's interest"; and (d) "any other criteria that may be prescribed are met".
-- s 25: "Despite section 7(3)(b)", a licence may be granted to a Singapore company to which the Government "has, before 1 April
-- 2015, issued a certificate of sponsorship".
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `applicant` IS AN Actor
    `meets or is likely to meet the Annex III, Article 4 standards` IS A BOOLEAN
    `will apply to the ISA for a corresponding contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was sponsored by the Government before 1 April 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the grant is in Singapore's interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets any prescribed criteria` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may grant the licence` IF
        `the applicant`'s `applicant` EQUALS `a Singapore company`
    AND `the applicant`'s `meets or is likely to meet the Annex III, Article 4 standards`
    AND (`the applicant`'s `will apply to the ISA for a corresponding contract` OR `the applicant`'s `was sponsored by the Government before 1 April 2015`)
    AND `the applicant`'s `the grant is in Singapore's interest`
    AND `the applicant`'s `meets any prescribed criteria`

-- s 12(2): "A licence may only be transferred to a Singapore company which (a) is eligible under section 7 to be granted a
-- licence; and (b) meets any other criteria that may be prescribed." (1): on the application of BOTH the licensee and the
-- intended transferee. INFERENCE: "eligible under section 7" is read here as the whole of s 7, including s 7(3).
GIVEN `the transferee` IS AN Applicant, `both applied` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets prescribed transfer criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer may be approved` IF
        `both applied`
    AND `the Minister may grant the licence` `the transferee`
    AND `meets prescribed transfer criteria`

§§ `13, 14 -- lapse, suspension and revocation`

-- s 13: a licence LAPSES when (a) the licensee "fails to enter into a corresponding ISA contract within 12 months (or such longer
-- period as the Minister may allow)" after grant or transfer; (b) the ISA contracts with "a person other than the licensee" for
-- the same resource in the same part of the Area; (c) "the corresponding ISA contract is terminated for any reason"; (d) the
-- licensee "is wound up or otherwise dissolved"; (e) any prescribed event.
GIVEN `months allowed by the Minister` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the period to obtain an ISA contract` MEANS
    IF `months allowed by the Minister` AT LEAST 12 THEN `months allowed by the Minister` ELSE 12

DECLARE Licence HAS
    `months since grant or transfer` IS A NUMBER
    `months allowed by the Minister for the contract` IS A NUMBER
    `ISA contract entered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ISA contracted with someone else for the same resource and part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ISA contract was terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ISA contract was suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licensee was wound up or dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a prescribed lapsing event occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licensee contravened the Act or a condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister finds the activities not properly carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister finds suspension or revocation in Singapore's interest` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the licence` IS A Licence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence lapses` IF
        (    (NOT `the licence`'s `ISA contract entered`)
         AND `the licence`'s `months since grant or transfer` GREATER THAN `the period to obtain an ISA contract` (`the licence`'s `months allowed by the Minister for the contract`))
    OR  `the licence`'s `the ISA contracted with someone else for the same resource and part`
    OR  `the licence`'s `the ISA contract was terminated`
    OR  `the licence`'s `the licensee was wound up or dissolved`
    OR  `the licence`'s `a prescribed lapsing event occurred`

-- s 14(1): the Minister MAY suspend or revoke if (a) the licensee "has contravened the provisions of this Act or the conditions
-- of the licence"; (b) "the corresponding ISA contract is suspended for any reason"; (c) the activities have not been, or will
-- not be, carried on "in a proper and satisfactory manner"; or (d) "it is in Singapore's interest".
-- A terminated ISA contract ends the licence automatically (s 13(c)); a suspended one only opens the Minister's discretion.
GIVEN `the licence` IS A Licence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may suspend or revoke` IF
        `the licence`'s `the licensee contravened the Act or a condition`
    OR  `the licence`'s `the ISA contract was suspended`
    OR  `the licence`'s `the Minister finds the activities not properly carried on`
    OR  `the licence`'s `the Minister finds suspension or revocation in Singapore's interest`

§§ `15 -- representations before suspension or revocation`

-- s 15(1): written notice of intention; (2) representations "within one month after receiving the notice ... (or such longer period
-- as the Minister may allow)"; (3) the Minister must consider them; (4) the final decision must be given in writing "within one
-- month after the end of the period in subsection (2)"; (5) it "takes effect 14 days (or such longer period as the Minister may
-- allow) after the date on which the licensee is informed".
GIVEN `months after the notice` IS A NUMBER, `longer months allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the representations are in time` IF
        `months after the notice` AT MOST 1
    OR  `months after the notice` AT MOST `longer months allowed`

GIVEN `longer days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days after being informed until the decision takes effect` MEANS
    IF `longer days allowed` AT LEAST 14 THEN `longer days allowed` ELSE 14

§§ `16 -- directions when a licence ends`

-- s 16(1): the section applies where "(a) a licence expires; (b) a licence is transferred under section 12; (c) a licence lapses
-- under section 13; or (d) a licensee has been informed under section 15(4) of the Minister's decision to revoke the licence".
-- Suspension is not on the list.
DECLARE Ending IS ONE OF
    `expiry`
    `transfer`
    `lapse`
    `revocation`
    `suspension`

GIVEN `the ending` IS AN Ending
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 16 applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the ending`
    WHEN `suspension` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 16(3): directions may be given to "(a) the licensee; (b) any director or senior manager of the licensee; or (c) if there is no
-- director or senior manager of the licensee who is able to comply ..., any person who was a director of the licensee in the period
-- of 6 months immediately preceding the date of the relevant event". A former senior manager is not in (c).
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the licensee itself`
    `a current director`
    `a current senior manager`
    `a former director`
    `a former senior manager`
    `a shareholder`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `months before the event they left` IS A NUMBER, `a current director or senior manager can comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be directed` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the licensee itself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a current director` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a current senior manager` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a former director` THEN (NOT `a current director or senior manager can comply`) AND `months before the event they left` AT MOST 6
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 16(6): a person who complies with a direction "is not liable for any loss or damage suffered by any other person as a result
-- of the compliance"; (7) not for an act "that purports to be in compliance with, but is not required by," the direction.
GIVEN `acted under a direction` IS A BOOLEAN, `the act was required by the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the compliance immunity applies` IF
    `acted under a direction` AND `the act was required by the direction`

§§ `10(4), 11(3), 16(5), 24(2)(g) -- financial penalties`

-- s 10(4): if the Minister "is satisfied that a licensee has breached any condition of its licence", a financial penalty "not
-- exceeding $40,000". s 11(3) and s 16(5): the same maximum for failing "without reasonable excuse" to comply with a direction.
-- A condition breach carries no reasonable-excuse qualifier.
DECLARE Failure IS ONE OF
    `breach of a licence condition`
    `failure to comply with a direction to a licensee`
    `failure to comply with a wind-down direction`

GIVEN `the failure` IS A Failure, `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a financial penalty may be imposed` IF
    CONSIDER `the failure`
    WHEN `breach of a licence condition` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOT `reasonable excuse`

GIVEN `the failure` IS A Failure
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS 40000

-- s 24(2)(g): regulations may provide "either, but not both" of a financial penalty not exceeding $40,000 or an offence punishable
-- with a fine not exceeding $40,000, for a specified provision.
GIVEN `has a financial penalty` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a regulation's sanction is within section 24(2)(g)` IF
        (`has a financial penalty` OR `is an offence`)
    AND (NOT (`has a financial penalty` AND `is an offence`))
    AND `amount` AT MOST 40000

§§ `21 -- officers, partners and members`

-- s 21(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an
-- officer; or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the officer's part, the officer as well as the body corporate shall be
-- guilty". (5): "officer" includes "any person purporting to act in any such capacity".
GIVEN `the body committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the body committed an offence` AND (`consent or connivance` OR `attributable to neglect`)
